Changes: reading blocks extracted into structured versions with stable IDs,
source element locators, explicit secondary status and language partitions.
The Wikipedia versions are excluded from analytical admission. The project
does not adopt the article's proposed historical language relationships,
translations, discovery completeness, or present locations as verified facts.

Historical transcriptions were encoded from printed pages. Spaces and dots
are project-normalized textual representations, not a facsimile of the
stone. Question marks, superscript alternatives, underlines, partial strokes
and font shapes require the attached scan; conservative line flags exclude
these readings from frequency pending independent collation. No current
reading or phonetic value is asserted by encoding a historical author's text.

Yves Duhoux 1982, Guarducci 1942, the Dreros editions, Kritzas and the Azoria
publications are bibliographic or research leads. Their modern critical
texts and images have not been redistributed or relicensed. The Arkalochori
object is linked from its shared disputed-object register, not admitted as
Eteocretan. Pinned corpus-family reports retain their original attribution
and native acceptance gates.

